    "description": "A separate desktop nav (base display:none, flex at the desktop reference viewport via a breakpoint class) sits between a brand anchor and an unrelated button cluster, with a separate mobile-only hamburger toggle further along in the header. The nav must convert in its OWN document position — between the brand and the button cluster, matching where it renders at the desktop viewport — not at the toggle's position past the unrelated buttons. Each item's anchor wraps an icon-plus-label pill in a single inner element (the shape core/navigation collapses); the pill's shared box/gap classes and the icon must both survive onto the generated navigation-link, or the item silently loses its size, its gap, and its icon while keeping only bare text.",
